## Week 7- 

### My Contributions
This week I continued developing Task 7. I focused on completing the nearest-neighbour search functionality and testing the implementation against 
the supplied ITN dataset. I used the R - tree spatial indexing method mentioned in the previous week to identify the closest road network to a given coordinate.
The method retrieves the corresponding ITN node identifier and coordinates, then calculates the distance between the input location and the selected node. I structured 
the method to return the node ID, coordinates, and distance, allowing its output to be reused by other parts of the application. This is particularly important for integrating 
Task 7 with Task 8, which requires the network node identifiers to calculate a route. Created a separate test file to test functionality. 

### Challenges and Learning 
I had several inconsistencies in naming, which caused issues with imports. I also encountered issues with debugging and implementation of the R- tree concept into physical code.
Working through these issues improved my understanding of file paths, external libraries, and virtual environments. I also developed a clearer understanding of how R-tree nearest-neighbour 
searching works and how the resulting node information can be used in network-based route planning.



